The {{nihongo|'''Nankō Port Town Line'''|南港ポートタウン線|Nankō Pōtotaun-sen}}, commonly known as the "New Tram", is an automated guideway transit (AGT) line in [[Okami|Okami (大紙)]], [[Okaiken]], operated by [[Okami Metro]]. It serves the reclaimed islands of the Okami Bay Area, connecting the residential districts of "Port Town" with the exhibition centers and ferry terminals. On system maps, the line is color-coded cerulean blue ({{Okami Metro color|P}}), and its stations use the prefix "P".

Unlike the heavy rail subway lines, the Nankō Port Town Line utilizes rubber-tyred automated trains running on an elevated concrete guideway. It functions as a crucial connector loop on the western edge of the city, linking the western terminus of the [[Chūō Line (Okami)|Chūō Line]] at [[Cosmosquare Station|Cosmosquare]] with the southern terminus of the [[Shitayanagi Line]] at [[Suminoe-Koen Station|Suminoe-Koen]].

==History==
Construction began in the late 1970s to serve the newly developed "Nankō" (South Port) residential new town. The first section between [[Nakafuto Station|Nakafuto]] and [[Suminoe-Koen Station|Suminoe-Koen]] opened on March 16, 1981.

The line was extended north to [[Cosmosquare Station|Cosmosquare]] in 1997 to connect with the Chūō Line and the new seaside business district. The line has operated with fully unmanned automated trains since 1991, following a system-wide upgrade to ATO (Automatic Train Operation).

